{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Behold, you.</b> A sign for the idols." "<b>From nothing.</b> Like \"nothing and breath,\" and it has no parallel in all of Scripture." "<b>Abomination, etc.</b> The meaning: \"a man of abomination\" will choose you, or \"for abomination\" he will choose you — one who worships you."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:26.056455921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}